From 0958223205e85133cd716dae9d30e90000264773 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:48:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Configurable button look and a PNG preview mode

Colours, height, corner radius, gaps and text/icon sizes of the buttons come
from the config (FontSize, IconSize, ButtonColor, ButtonActiveColor,
ButtonHeight, ButtonRadius, ButtonSpacing, GroupSpacing, EscWidth); without
them the upstream look stays. Per button, Width gives a fixed width and
Group = true a wider gap before it, so that rows can be laid out like the
macOS Touch Bar (narrow Esc, grouped keys).

Drawing and touch use one layout function now: before, hit() ignored the
room reserved for pixel shift and the two could disagree by up to 11 px. A
touch in a gap goes to the nearer button instead of nowhere. A partial
redraw clears and updates the whole button column.

TINY_DFR_RENDER_PNG=<file> draws the configured layers into a PNG (base
layer, the same with a pressed button, the Fn layer) without touching DRM
or input, for checking a layout before installing it.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
